    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d809">

                <pb facs="0902" n="892" sameAs="frus:frus1943China/pg892"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">751.93/104: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-10-19T15:00:00+07:00">October 19, 1943—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 19—12:13 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1980. (1). Reference Department’s 1461, October 11. The Counselor of the
                        Embassy<anchor n="6" xml:id="d809-f1"/> called on Vice Foreign Minister Hoo
                    on October 18 on another matter and during conversation inquired as to
                    Sino-French relations, mentioned report in question and expressed interest as
                    requested. Hoo stated that time for evacuations of premises is being extended
                    one month to enable French employees to make arrangements for travel to North
                    Africa.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d809-f1" n="6" xml:id="d809-f1-content">
